As the probable originator of the vegetarian valkyrie, I suppose I
should post a few pointers for any who wish to follow. =)

Viable food:
  food rations, C-Rations, K-Rations, pancakes, cream pies, apples, melons,
  pears, bananas, fortune cookies, mold corpes, jelly corpses, blob corpses,
  fungi corpses, pudding corpses, tins of spinish (or any of the preceding
  corpses), and of course your customizable 'fruit' (which I called 'tofu',
  of course)

Intrinsics:
  gaining intrinsics is a pain... but it is possible to get every last one
  of 'em (though a few you have to rely on items for).
  Becoming the Envoy of Balance is almost a must... as it is very hard to
  get fire resistance by the time you need it. Disintigration resistance
  is the only totally impossible one (for which you have to rely on
  an item (therefore BDSM becomes a must))
  Some of them are only possible if you do the ring eating thing (and then
  only if it is of an edible variety) This applies to teleport control,
  teleport, conflict, aggrevate monster, polymorph, polymorph control,
  protection from shape changers and maybe regeneration (can you
  gain this intrinsicly from eating the ring? come to think of it, if
  you eat a ring of levitation, could you get permanent levitation?)
  Sleep resistance seems impossible, but I finally got it around level 43
  after eating a quivering blob.
  Telepathy also seems impossible, but if you are really lucky, sometimes
  your god will give it to you when you're praying. (honest)
  The remainder of the resistances can be got from various fungis, molds,
  jellies and puddings, et al.

Equipment:
  A few items are a must. BDSM and a Cloak of MP and a SoR. The sooner
  you get the shield, the better chances you have. (A wand of sleep will
  be your downfall otherwise) A helm of telepathy or an amulet of ESP
  are also very important (preferably the helm) and the GoP are handy
  since you can't get your strength up by eating giant corpses.
  A Bag of Holding is also very important, cause you will have to
  pack around ALOT of food. You may think you have too much food, but
  believe me, you'll end up eating it. (and if you're one of those
  types who like to use regen or conflict or teleport about, or any
  other food using type activities, you'll need it even more)
  I've heard folks mention a horn of plenty, but I've never seen one,
  and don't believe in using spoiler information. =)

  The quest artifact is useless. I assume it does something... but
  nothing worthwhile. Can't even use it to look for traps, so even
  that idea whent kaput.  8(


